
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:help@

%9Parameters:%9

    The command to display the documentation for; if no argument is given, the
    list of commands will be displayed.

%9Description:%9

    Displays the documentation for the given command.

    Help files are read from the help directory in your configuration
    directory (~/.erssi/help) first, then from the directories in the
    help_path setting. Put a file named after a command there to add help
    for a script command or to replace the built-in text.

%9Examples:%9

    /HELP
    /HELP AWAY
    /HELP CONNECT

%9References:%9

    https://irssi.org
    https://github.com/irssi

%9See also:%9 CONNECT, MSG, NETWORK, SERVER

